Theorem PL-7: TRMC normalization (Step 3a) detects tail-recursive constructor candidates, carrying the ContextBehavior 4-field record

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS pipeline is a 12-step strictly-ordered sequence per
      Annex E §AIMS + arc.md sec-Pipeline. PL-7 is the first rule of the
      §07.4 TRMC cluster (PL-7 through PL-11), governing Step 3a TRMC
      normalization detection.
    - PL-7 statement (per Annex E §AIMS PL-7 + Leijen & Lorenzen,
      "Tail Recursion Modulo Context", JFP 2025): Step 3a TRMC normalization
      SHALL detect tail-recursive functions returning constructor
      applications. The `ContextBehavior` contract on `MemoryContract` tracks
      four fields: `preserves_context`, `consumes_hole`,
      `requires_unique_context`, `may_resume_nonlinearly`.
    - PL-7 type signature (per Pipeline.proof lines 59-65, the sorry
      obligation this theorem discharges):
        type : Function -> Option ContextRegion
        Step 3a TRMC normalization detects tail-recursive fns returning
        constructor applications; ContextBehavior 4-field record carries
        preserves_context / consumes_hole / requires_unique_context /
        may_resume_nonlinearly.
    - Shipped detection driver: ori_arc::aims::intraprocedural::
      post_convergence::detect_trmc_candidates (compiler/
      ori_arc/src/aims/intraprocedural/post_convergence.rs lines 442-526).
      The admissibility filter that selects a `Construct` as a TRMC candidate:
        (a) the constructor kind is a struct or enum variant —
            `matches!(ctor, CtorKind::Struct(_) | CtorKind::EnumVariant { .. })`
            (post_convergence.rs lines 484-487); tuple / closure ctors
            (NonReusable shape) are NOT candidates;
        (b) at least one field argument was produced by a self-recursive call —
            `args.iter().any(|arg| recursive_defs.contains(arg))`
            (post_convergence.rs lines 493-497), where `recursive_defs` is the
            set of variables defined by `Apply`/`Invoke` whose callee is the
            current function (collected via collect_recursive_call_sites,
            post_convergence.rs lines 449-450);
        (c) the constructor destination is `Uniqueness::Unique` at the mutation
            point — `if state.uniqueness != Uniqueness::Unique { continue; }`
            (post_convergence.rs lines 511-514). This is the SOLE enforced
            soundness gate (Lemma 2, Leijen & Lorenzen JFP 2025) — no other
            references exist at the mutation point so the in-place hole fill is
            safe.
      When all three hold, the constructor's shape is upgraded to
      `ShapeClass::ContextHole` (post_convergence.rs lines 516-517:
      `state_map.set_var_shape(*dst, ShapeClass::ContextHole)`).
    - Shipped ContextBehavior record: ori_arc::aims::contract::context::
      ContextBehavior (compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/contract/
      context.rs lines 33-50) carries EXACTLY four boolean fields:
        - `preserves_context` (context.rs line 37)
        - `consumes_hole` (context.rs line 40)
        - `requires_unique_context` (context.rs line 44)
        - `may_resume_nonlinearly` (context.rs line 49)
      Re-exported as ori_arc::aims::contract::ContextBehavior (contract/mod.rs
      line 25) and carried on `MemoryContract.context_behavior` (contract/
      mod.rs line 53).
    - Locality is deliberately NOT a detection gate: TRMC constructors are
      typically returned (`HeapEscaping`), which is expected — the whole point
      of TRMC is to build the result in place and return it
      (post_convergence.rs lines 433-435 + 503-505). Function-level
      `may_share` is logged but NOT enforced (post_convergence.rs lines
      455-466 + 507-510) because the `HeapEscaping -> may_share` accumulation
      rule makes every TRMC candidate trigger `may_share`; the per-variable
      `Unique` guarantee is the actual soundness condition.

  Soundness property:
    Forall function F processed by Step 3a TRMC normalization, and forall
    `Construct` instruction c in F.
      Let admitted(c) = Step 3a upgrades c's shape to ContextHole.
      Two conjuncts SHALL hold:

      (P1) Detection scope:
        admitted(c) iff (c.ctor in {Struct, EnumVariant})
                      AND (exists arg in c.args. arg in recursive_defs(F))
                      AND (uniqueness(c.dst) = Unique).
        No constructor outside this conjunction is upgraded to ContextHole; no
        constructor inside it is skipped.

      (P2) ContextBehavior record shape:
        The `ContextBehavior` contract carries exactly the four boolean fields
        {preserves_context, consumes_hole, requires_unique_context,
        may_resume_nonlinearly} — no more, no fewer.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part constructive discharge corresponding to (P1) and (P2), by
    case analysis over the constructor-admissibility grid (case_analysis-led
    per the §00 PL row) + structural confirmation of the contract record shape.

    Part (P1) — Detection scope (case analysis over the admissibility grid):

      The verifier models the shipped `detect_trmc_candidates` filter as the
      conjunction
        pl7_is_detected(s) = s.is_struct_or_enum_variant
                             AND s.has_recursive_arg
                             AND s.dst_unique
      and exercises it over a five-row constructor grid spanning every
      single-conjunct failure plus the all-hold case:

        Row 1 struct_recursive_unique — all three hold -> DETECTED
        Row 2 enum_variant_recursive_unique — all three hold -> DETECTED
        Row 3 tuple_ctor_rejected — ctor not struct/enum -> REJECTED
        Row 4 struct_no_recursive_arg — no recursive arg -> REJECTED
        Row 5 struct_recursive_non_unique — dst not Unique -> REJECTED

      For each row the verifier asserts pl7_is_detected agrees with the row's
      expected detection. Rows 1-2 are the positive cases (the two ReusableCtor
      shapes); rows 3-5 are the three negative cases, one per dropped conjunct,
      mirroring the shipped early-`continue` guards (post_convergence.rs lines
      485-487 for the ctor-kind gate, 495-497 for the recursive-arg gate,
      512-514 for the uniqueness gate). The case-by-case agreement discharges
      (P1).

    Part (P2) — ContextBehavior record shape (structural confirmation):

      The verifier enumerates the four field names
      {preserves_context, consumes_hole, requires_unique_context,
      may_resume_nonlinearly} and asserts the count is exactly 4, matching the
      shipped struct (context.rs lines 33-50). A field added or removed in the
      shipped record would diverge the count and Fail the check. (P2)
      discharged.

    Coverage gate — constructor-admissibility enumeration:

      The verifier discharges exactly 5 constructor-admissibility sites
      (require_count("PL-7", 5, ...)). Coverage axes:
        Detection scope (P1): the 5 grid rows — 2 positive (struct + enum
          variant), 3 negative (non-ctor-kind, no-recursive-arg, non-unique).
        Record shape (P2): the 4-field ContextBehavior count check.

    Negative-direction witness — non-struct ctor rejected:

      A tuple- or closure-shaped constructor (NonReusable shape) with a
      recursive field arg and a Unique dst is NOT a TRMC candidate — the
      shipped filter gates on `CtorKind::Struct | CtorKind::EnumVariant`
      (post_convergence.rs lines 485-487). The verifier's row 3
      (tuple_ctor_rejected) pins this: a non-struct/enum ctor with the other
      two conjuncts satisfied still yields pl7_is_detected = false.

    Negative-direction witness — non-unique dst rejected:

      A struct constructor with a recursive arg but a `dst` whose uniqueness is
      MaybeShared or Shared is rejected by the Lemma 2 gate
      (post_convergence.rs lines 511-514). The verifier's row 5
      (struct_recursive_non_unique) pins this: the sole enforced soundness
      condition is per-variable Unique; dropping it blocks detection.

    Cycle-soundness witness — PL-7 antecedes the rest of the TRMC cluster:

      PL-7 (detection scope + ContextBehavior record) is the antecedent of
      PL-8 (candidate predicate refines the detection conjunction with the
      context-region span), PL-9 (rewrite of detected candidates), PL-10
      (structural verification of the rewrite), and PL-11 (ContextBehavior
      initialization + join over the record PL-7 introduces). PL-7 consumes no
      output of any later TRMC rule. The dependency chain is acyclic:
        PL-7 --> PL-8 (predicate over the detected candidate set)
        PL-7 --> PL-9 (rewrite of detected candidates)
        PL-7 --> PL-11 (join over the ContextBehavior record)
      PL-7 is the leaf of this dependency tree.

    Algorithm-citation declaration:
      property: TRMC candidate detection scope — a Construct is a
                           context-hole candidate iff struct/enum-variant ctor
                           + self-recursive field arg + Unique dst; the
                           ContextBehavior contract carries exactly four
                           boolean fields
      published: Leijen & Lorenzen, "Tail Recursion Modulo Context",
                           JFP 2025 (the four-field constructor-context
                           behavior; Lemma 2 uniqueness soundness for in-place
                           hole fill); the Perceus reuse lineage (Reinking,
                           Lorenzen, Leijen & de Moura, PLDI 2021) cited in
                           Annex E §AIMS prior-art table
      determinism: deterministic — detect_trmc_candidates scans blocks
                           in index order, applies a fixed three-conjunct
                           filter, and sets ContextHole shape deterministically;
                           no schedule or hash-order freedom
      reference impl: ori_arc::aims::intraprocedural::post_convergence::
                           detect_trmc_candidates (post_convergence.rs lines
                           442-526: ctor-kind gate lines 485-487, recursive-arg
                           gate lines 493-497, uniqueness gate lines 511-514,
                           ContextHole upgrade lines 516-517) +
                           ori_arc::aims::contract::context::ContextBehavior
                           (context.rs lines 33-50)

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY — confirms the detection-scope conjunction
        and the ContextBehavior record shape over the §07.4 TRMC structural
        model per section_07::verify_pl7_trmc_detect_candidate; agrees with
        case_analysis on the constructive verifier)
      case_analysis (LED — per the §00 PL-row pair per the proof-checker design-proof-
        checker-design.md:102, the TRMC cluster is case_analysis-heavy; the
        verifier discharges (P1) via the five-row constructor-admissibility
        grid — 2 positive ReusableCtor rows + 3 negative single-conjunct-drop
        rows — and (P2) via the four-field record-shape count; constructive,
        NOT gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_07 case_analysis-led discharge of PL-7 via the constructor-admissibility grid — (P1) detect_trmc_candidates admits a Construct as a ContextHole candidate iff struct/enum-variant ctor (post_convergence.rs lines 485-487) AND self-recursive field arg (lines 493-497) AND Unique dst (lines 511-514), verified over a five-row grid (2 positive ReusableCtor rows + 3 negative single-conjunct-drop rows), and (P2) the ContextBehavior contract carries exactly the four fields preserves_context / consumes_hole / requires_unique_context / may_resume_nonlinearly (context.rs lines 33-50); grounded in the shipped Step 3a detection driver + the 4-field record; structural_induction PRIMARY confirms over the same verifier
